#: includes/views/help-tab.php:78
msgid "Set your delivery window"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:79
msgid "On the Delivery tab, enter the minimum and maximum days a parcel takes to arrive after you hand it to the carrier. Set both to the same number for a single date instead of a range. Use 0 for same-day delivery."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:82
msgid "Set your order cutoff"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:83
msgid "Orders placed before this time go out the same day. Anything after it moves to the next dispatch day."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:86
msgid "Tick your non-dispatch days"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:87
msgid "The weekdays you do not send orders out, usually Saturday and Sunday. They are never counted toward the estimate."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:90
msgid "Add your holidays"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:91
msgid "Single dates or date ranges you are closed. Tick \"Repeats every year\" for fixed holidays such as Christmas."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:94
msgid "Choose where it appears"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:95
msgid "The Display tab controls product pages, shop archives, cart, and checkout. The Style tab controls wording and colours. The live preview updates as you type."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:106
msgid "How the date is worked out"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:109
msgid "QuickShipD keeps the day you dispatch separate from the days a parcel spends in transit."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:114
msgid "Start from today"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:115
msgid "If the cutoff time has already passed, move to tomorrow."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:119
msgid "Find the dispatch day"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:120
msgid "If that day is a non-dispatch day or a holiday, roll forward until it is not."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:124
msgid "Count the transit days"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:125
msgid "Count forward from the dispatch day, skipping non-dispatch days and holidays."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:130
#: includes/views/help-tab.php:218
msgid "Worked example"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:131
msgid "Weekends off, delivery 1 to 2 days, a customer orders on Saturday. Nothing ships at the weekend, so the dispatch day rolls to Monday. One to two days after Monday gives Tuesday to Wednesday. Monday is never shown as the arrival date, because that is the day the parcel leaves you."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:134
msgid "The countdown is hidden on days you do not dispatch, because beating the cutoff on those days cannot change the date."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:139
msgid "On the Display tab, open Product delivery date to choose which date customers see on product pages, variations, and shop archives."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:143
msgid "Show a single earliest date, even when your delivery window is a range. The default wording becomes “Get it as soon as” and the countdown uses the same date."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:146
msgid "Latest date or delivery range"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:147
msgid "Latest date shows a single date at the end of the delivery window. Delivery range keeps the existing earliest-to-latest display. Your custom message templates are respected."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:151
msgid "Enable this to use the fastest eligible WooCommerce shipping rate for one unit of the product and the customer’s destination. Configure each method’s delivery days in WooCommerce → Settings → Shipping. Local pickup is excluded. If the destination is unknown or no eligible rates are available, the estimate uses your store and product settings."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:152
msgid "The final rate can change with quantity, coupons, and cart contents. When fastest shipping is enabled, product estimates show “With the fastest shipping option.” Cart and checkout follow the selected method."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:153
msgid "The live preview shows the chosen date style using your timing settings. It does not calculate shipping rates because there is no product or customer destination in the preview."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:162
msgid "Same-day dispatch and delivery"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:165
msgid "Delivery days are counted after dispatch, so 0 days means the parcel arrives on the day it goes out. Set the minimum to 0 and the cutoff becomes your same-day deadline."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:167
msgid "Pick your numbers"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:172
msgid "What you promise"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:173
msgid "Minimum"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:174
msgid "Maximum"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:179
msgid "Always same day"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:184
msgid "Same day, sometimes next day"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:189
msgid "Next day at the earliest"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:196
msgid "Set it up"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:200
msgid "Set minimum delivery days to 0"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:201
msgid "On the Delivery tab. Set the maximum to 0 as well for a single date, or to 1 if a late order might slip to tomorrow."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:204
msgid "Set the cutoff to your last dispatch run"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:205
msgid "This is the moment same-day stops being possible. If your courier collects at 11am, set 11:00. Orders after it automatically move to the next dispatch day, so you never promise a delivery you cannot make."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:208
msgid "Match the non-dispatch days to your opening days"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:209
msgid "Delivering seven days a week? Untick every day. Closed at weekends? Leave Saturday and Sunday ticked, and weekend orders will quote the next working day instead."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:212
msgid "Say so in the wording"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:213
msgid "On the Style tab, a countdown line such as \"Order within {countdown} for delivery today\" turns the cutoff into a reason to buy now. Keep the countdown switched on for this."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:219
msgid "Minimum 0, maximum 0, cutoff 11:00, closed at weekends. An order at 10:30 on Monday shows Monday, with 30 minutes left on the countdown. At 11:30 the same order shows Tuesday and the countdown disappears. An order on Saturday shows Monday, because nothing is dispatched at the weekend."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:222
msgid "Same-day can also be set for one product only, or for one shipping method such as local delivery, using the overrides described in the Overrides section."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:231
msgid "Where the estimate shows"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:236
msgid "Product page"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:237
msgid "Full estimate with icon and the cutoff countdown. Variable products update as the shopper picks a variation."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:240
msgid "Shop and archives"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:240
msgid "off by default"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:241
msgid "Compact estimate, no countdown."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:244
msgid "Cart"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:245
msgid "An \"Est. Delivery\" line under each item. Works on the classic and the block cart."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:248
msgid "Checkout"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:249
msgid "A summary row above shipping on the classic checkout. On the block checkout the per-item line shows instead."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:252
msgid "Emails and orders"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:253
msgid "Saved onto the order line at checkout, so it stays fixed on the order record. Display > Orders & Emails controls whether it is saved at all, and which emails it appears in."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:268
msgid "Place the estimate yourself anywhere on the site. This is the answer whenever a page builder such as Elementor or Divi builds its own product layout, never fires the standard WooCommerce hooks, and the estimate does not appear on its own."
